<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bhopal Agency</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bhopal Agency was a political agency within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-india-agency">Central India Agency</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-india">British India</a>, supervising Bhopal State and a group of smaller states in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a>, among them Rajgarh, Narsinghgarh, Kurwai, Basoda, Pathari and Mohammadgarh. A British political agent based at Sehore oversaw their relations with the government. After independence the states acceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and were merged into Madhya Bharat and Bhopal State, now part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bhopal-agency.jpg" alt="Bhopal Agency" width="320" height="261" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: J G Bartholomew · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Central_India_Agency_1909.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
